# English translation supplement for the self-test CodeSystem.
#
# This file demonstrates a translation the IG Publisher ACTUALLY renders: a
# supplement for a CodeSystem (one of StructureDefinition / CodeSystem /
# Questionnaire — the only resource types the toolchain translates today; see
# skills/ig-translate/SKILL.md and docs/recipes/add-translation.md).
#
# Naming (mandatory): input/translations/<lang>/<ResourceType>-<id>.po, wired via
# the `translation-sources` parameter in sushi-config.yaml. A wrong name (e.g.
# ValueSet-... or menu.po) is silently IGNORED by the Publisher.
#
# Each msgid MUST match, byte for byte, the German source text in
# fsh-generated/resources/CodeSystem-selftest-palette.json (regenerate with
# `sushi .` and copy the exact string, umlauts included). msgstr is the English
# rendering shown on the /en/ CodeSystem page. The German source is never edited
# by translation work — the supplement is purely additive.
#
# Note: CodeSystem.title ("Selbsttest-Palette") is deliberately NOT translated
# here — `title` is not in the toolchain's translatable set, so a supplement for
# it would be ignored. The title therefore stays German on /en/, while the
# description and concept texts below do switch to English — exactly what the
# rendering table predicts.

#: CodeSystem.description
msgid "Zwei beliebige Codes, damit die Selbsttest-IG eine CodeSystem-Seite rendert; kein MII-Artefakt."
msgstr "Two arbitrary codes so the self-test IG renders a CodeSystem page; not an MII artifact."

#: CodeSystem.concept[0].display
msgid "Primärfarbe"
msgstr "Primary colour"

#: CodeSystem.concept[0].definition
msgid "Platzhalter für den Steckplatz der primären Markenfarbe der Vorlage."
msgstr "Placeholder for the template's primary brand-colour slot."

#: CodeSystem.concept[1].display
msgid "Akzentfarbe"
msgstr "Accent colour"

#: CodeSystem.concept[1].definition
msgid "Platzhalter für den Steckplatz der Akzentfarbe der Vorlage."
msgstr "Placeholder for the template's accent-colour slot."
